+## R18 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 18)
+
+All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only, at 1440 × 900 and device scale one. Panel round 18 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.
+
+- **Backstop role (R18-MIMAR-02, R18-GPT-04; Fadel's tiebreak):** pixels decide visibility, not AA. Where the CSS pass resolves the colours, pixels fail a line only when its strongest ink pixel is under 1.5:1 or it has fewer than three ink pixels; where it does not (background images, filters, blends, translucent covers), the 90th-percentile ink must reach 3:1. Only opaque covers (replaced elements, background colours at 90% or more opacity) obscure. Executed: Lato, Inter and Inter Tight at weights 100-400, 12-48 px, in #1a1a1a, #595959 and #767676 (180 combinations, 0 failures), a 3% white layer, the honest-pattern set below. UNTESTED: other fonts, hinting and device scale 2; text over photographs where the CSS pass is unknown and the photo is pale (graded at 3:1 by pixels, so a thin weight there can still fail); a cover between 3% and 90% opacity is graded by pixels at 3:1; only the 3% layer and the gradient fade were executed.
+- **Lines from text ranges (R18-GPT-03/07):** each text node's word ranges are grouped into line boxes; the middle 60% of each line box is sampled. UNTESTED: vertical writing modes, ruby, text with negative letter spacing or overlapping lines (line-height under 1), pseudo-element text, SVG text, text nodes longer than 4,000 words (the rest is not grouped).
+- **Clipped text (R18-MIMAR-01, R18-GPT-05):** text clipped to nothing by an ancestor that cannot be scrolled is not displayed (`textHidden`); text outside a scrollable ancestor's scrollport is scrolled into view (vertical and horizontal), and every scrolled ancestor is restored afterwards. Executed: carousel with and without autoplay, max-height accordion, script-opened accordion (JavaScript-off mismatch), app shell, horizontal tab strip. UNTESTED: `overflow: hidden` panels that script scrolls (treated as not scrollable, so their other text is hidden); `contain: paint` and `clip-path` on an ancestor as clippers (not used for hiding decisions; clip-path is caught by pixels); scroll snapping and scroll-driven animations that react to inner scrolling; nested scrollers more than two deep; text hidden this way in every rendering and in every declared state is never graded (that is the intended scope: declared states grade it).
+- **Coverage (R18-GPT-06):** target-directed scan, at most 300 steps and four passes; early stop or growth after the last pass is INCOMPLETE. Executed: a 40,000 px page, an IntersectionObserver footer, an endless list (INCOMPLETE at a 25-step bound), the real built site (12 and 8 steps). UNTESTED: virtualised lists that remove earlier rows (targets no longer in the document are not graded), pages where every step adds content (they stop at the bound; estimated under a minute per rendering from the 25-step run), content that appears only after a timer with page scripts on and no scrolling.
+- **Copy deck (R18-GPT-01, R18-GPT-02 P3):** a slot's optional `ariaLabel` (or a variant's) approves the accessible name separately; a name identical to the displayed value counts once; option labels are screened. UNTESTED: `aria-labelledby` names (not matched to the deck), `aria-description`, accessible names on display:contents elements.
+
